## Normalization

Pipeline (`onomatron.scraper.normalize`): `clean_name` → `is_name_like` →
`dedupe_names` (case-insensitive, first occurrence wins — sources are ordered
so Wikipedia beats external sources on duplicates) → `sanitize_for_model`
(lowercase, split full names on spaces, drop anything with digits/symbols,
latin letters only). Only the final `names.txt` is sanitized; the consolidated
`data/interim/names.jsonl` keeps the original forms.

## Splits

The benchmark splits **by name** (never by n-gram) into train/val/test =
80/10/10 with seed 42 (`onomatron.data.split_names`). Full protocol and
results: [onomatron-benchmark](https://huggingface.co/{{ benchmark_repo }}).

